],"tariffs":[0,0,0,0.0],"pricing_power":[0,0,0,0.0],"cost_cuts":[0,0,0,0.0],"guidance":[0,0,0,0.0,{"raise":0,"reaffirm":0,"cut":0}],"ai_disruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":0.2555,"r5":0.2689,"r20":0.4291,"r1_spy":0.2556,"r5_spy":0.252,"r20_spy":0.3746,"r1_sector":0.2475,"r5_sector":0.2196,"r20_sector":0.2607,"etf":"XLK"}},{"id":"NXPI 2026 Q3","t":"NXPI","d":"2026-10-27","time":null,"w":7316,"n":50,"url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/27/nxp-nxpi-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","lens":{"theater":[0,0,0,0.0],"cinema":[0,0,0,0.0],"imax":[0,0,0,0.0],"streaming":[0,0,0,0.0],"dtc":[0,0,0,0.0],"ai_spend":[3,2,0,4.17],"tariffs":[0,0,0,0.0],"pricing_power":[3,3,0,4.17],"cost_cuts":[0,0,0,0.0],"guidance":[0,0,0,0.0,{"raise":0,"reaffirm":0,"cut":0}],"ai_disruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":-0.0071,"r5":0.0366,"r1_spy":-0.0106,"r5_spy":0.0565,"r1_sector":-0.0151,"r5_sector":0.1051,"etf":"XLK"}}],"quotes":[{"c":"NXPI 2020 Q2","e":"nxpi","d":"2020-07-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Peter Kelly","x":"The actions taken include the elimination of annual merit increases and incentives and effective hiring freeze, including replacements as well as salary cuts for executives.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2020 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2021-02-02","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Peter Kelly","x":"It's unfortunate that some of our suppliers are attempting to use the current tight supply environment as a short-term opportunity to raise prices, which we will clearly have to pass on.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2020 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2021-02-02","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Peter Kelly","x":"Having said that, we however seen price increases.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2021 Q2","e":"nxpi","d":"2021-08-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Peter Kelly","x":"Yes, it's -- we are not a commodity company, we don't raise prices when times are tight and reduce them when times are not tight.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2021 Q2","e":"nxpi","d":"2021-08-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Toshiya Hari","x":"We read about price increases from the foundries going forward.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2021 Q3","e":"nxpi","d":"2021-11-02","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"It's really just important that the leading concept and philosophy of all of this is that the price increase is just matching the input costs increase, and that's it.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2021 Q3","e":"nxpi","d":"2021-11-02","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Stacy Rasgon","x":"I guess, understanding that we're maybe coming off a higher base now, at least on raising price because of the input cost increases, do you foresee like a similar type of long-term pricing behavior that'll be built into the long-term contracts?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2021 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2022-02-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"So we do absolutely stick to the policy I've talked about before, which is that, of course, we are passing on the increased input cost and raise prices to our customers along with that.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2021 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2022-02-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Christopher Caso","x":"One is, obviously, we've seen foundry price increases announced last year.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2022 Q1","e":"nxpi","d":"2022-05-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"We are compensating our input cost increases with price increases to our customers.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2022 Q1","e":"nxpi","d":"2022-05-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"But our principle stance that if that happens, we will raise prices to protect our gross margins accordingly.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2022 Q3","e":"nxpi","d":"2022-11-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"And seeing how the supply-demand imbalance in our core markets is moving into next year, I guess, it is reasonable to assume that we will continue to raise prices also next year.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2023 Q1","e":"nxpi","d":"2023-05-02","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"This includes the ongoing secular adoption of xEV drivetrains and ADAS as well as NXP-specific content and price increases.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2023 Q1","e":"nxpi","d":"2023-05-02","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"So from that perspective, there will continue to be price increases this year.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2023 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2024-02-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"Full year revenue was $2.35 billion, down 13% year-on-year, a reflection of our tight channel management in a cyclically weak end market offsetting price increases.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2023 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2024-02-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bill Betz","x":"We expect stock-based compensation, which is not included in our non-GAAP guidance to be $127 million higher-than-normal, driven by our restructuring activities taken in Q4 as we continue to refine the portfolio.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2024 Q2","e":"nxpi","d":"2024-07-23","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"So when we have now a little lower outlook than we had before, it is just that we do a little less into the channel than what we would have planned earlier.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2024 Q3","e":"nxpi","d":"2024-11-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Francois-Xavier Bouvignies","x":"…trade-off between market share and gross margin, for example, would you consider like to exit some product as soon as you see something that doesn't play your way or cost saving program as well, given the very long down cycle, is it something that you consider as well potentially just strategy?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2024 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2025-02-04","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Vivek Arya","x":"There's a lot of talk of tariffs, et cetera, this year.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2024 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2025-02-04","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"And as Vivek alluded to, I mean, let's see what the tariffs will do to all of this, we can’t say.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2024 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2025-02-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bill Betz","x":"The sequential decline is driven by restructuring the business and lower variable compensation.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2024 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2025-02-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bill Betz","x":"First, as you can see, we have taken some restructuring charges in Q4 as we are creating space for our recent acquisitions to prevent dilution and to ensure we stay within our long-term operating expense model.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2025 Q1","e":"nxpi","d":"2025-04-29","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"We believe there is an inflection point in the industrial and IoT markets which is creating demand for intelligent edge AI compute solutions.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2025 Q1","e":"nxpi","d":"2025-04-29","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"Kinara is the AI edge compute, which I just discussed briefly on the call.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2025 Q1","e":"nxpi","d":"2025-04-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"We are operating in a very uncertain environment influenced by tariffs with volatile direct and indirect effects.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2025 Q1","e":"nxpi","d":"2025-04-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Kurt Sievers","x":"As of today, the direct impact of the current tariffs is immaterial to our financials.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2025 Q1","e":"nxpi","d":"2025-04-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bill Betz","x":"The sequential increase is driven by the normal annual merit increases and the previously disclosed annual license payment modestly offset by our ongoing restructuring to make room for the three pending acquisitions.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2025 Q1","e":"nxpi","d":"2025-04-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bill Betz","x":"After closing these acquisitions, our ongoing restructuring actions are intended to enable NXP to get into its stated long-term operating expense model of 23% in the second half of 2025.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"NXPI 2025 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2026-02-03","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Bill Betz","x":"Obviously, we'll always have leverage on the SG&A side of the house, but the investments that are required for SDVs and physical AI and where we want to take the company, we want to keep that at that 16% level, I would say, to make sure that we can capture that growth, that long-term growth that…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/nxp-nxpi-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"NXPI 2025 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2026-02-03","l":"ai_spend","r":"analyst","s":"William Stein","x":"And as a follow-up, there's a rapid growth area in semis, we all know, not just endpoint physical AI, but data center AI.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/nxp-nxpi-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"NXPI 2025 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2026-02-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Bill Betz","x":"Obviously, if we get any inflationary costs that we can't offset internally, we will protect our gross margins and pass those on to our customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/nxp-nxpi-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"NXPI 2025 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2026-02-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Matthew Prisco","x":"And have you seen any impact to date from component price increases potentially pressuring unit demand there?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/nxp-nxpi-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"NXPI 2025 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2026-02-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bill Betz","x":"The primary increase sequentially is driven by our 2 new acquisitions, where we continue to make space for our strategic investments, offset by restructuring actions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/nxp-nxpi-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"NXPI 2025 Q4","e":"nxpi","d":"2026-02-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bill Betz","x":"Consequentl